        {
          "id": "prm_ticket",
          "slug": "ticket-classifier",
          "name": "Ticket classifier",
          "description": "Classify support tickets into { billing · account · product · other }.",
          "purpose": "Classify support tickets into one of: billing, account, product, other. Short, lowercase, deterministic.",
          "readme": "# Ticket classifier\n\nA production prompt that routes incoming support tickets into **billing**, **account**, **product**, or **other**. The canonical branch is optimised for *single-word, lowercase* output so the downstream router can switch on it without regex gymnastics.\n\n## Contract\n\n- **Input**: one ticket body (`{{ticket}}`).\n- **Output**: exactly one word — `billing` | `account` | `product` | `other`.\n- **Ambiguity rule**: when two labels plausibly apply, pick the one tied to the user's immediate blocker. When no label applies, return `other`.\n\n## Shipping policy\n\n- `main` is what the router calls in production.\n- Changes land via a **Proposed change** with the `support-tickets` dataset attached as evidence.\n- A release is cut whenever the canonical head changes. Release notes are generated from every intervening change summary.\n",
          "canonicalBranchId": "br_main",
          "createdAt": 1713792000000,
          "updatedAt": 1713878400000,
          "branches": [
            { "id": "br_main",       "name": "main",          "headVersionId": "ver_2", "createdFromVersionId": null,    "status": "active",  "createdAt": 1713792000000, "color": "#6366f1" },
            { "id": "br_few_shot",   "name": "few-shot",      "headVersionId": "ver_5", "createdFromVersionId": "ver_2", "status": "active",  "createdAt": 1713805000000, "color": "#10b981" },
